**`ElggObject` is now abstract** — you can no longer create `ElggObject` entities directly. Every object must use a subclass.

```php
// Before (6.x):
$entity = new ElggObject();
$entity->subtype = 'my_subtype';
$entity->save();

// After (7.x): Must have a registered entity class
class MyEntity extends ElggObject {
    public const SUBTYPE = 'my_subtype';
    protected function initializeAttributes() {
        parent::initializeAttributes();
        $this->attributes['subtype'] = self::SUBTYPE;
    }
}

// In elgg-plugin.php:
'entities' => [
    [
        'type' => 'object',
        'subtype' => 'my_subtype',
        'class' => MyEntity::class,
    ],
],

// Usage:
$entity = new MyEntity();
$entity->save();
```

Search for direct ElggObject instantiation:
```bash
grep -rn 'new ElggObject\b\|new \\ElggObject\b' classes/ views/ actions/ --include='*.php'
```

Also check factory patterns and tests.

CSS Crush preprocessing has been completely removed from Elgg 7.x. CSS files are served as-is.

**What breaks:**
- CSS Crush variables (`$(varname)`) no longer work → use CSS custom properties (`var(--elgg-varname)`)
- CSS Crush nesting no longer works → use native CSS nesting (supported in PHP 8.3+ target browsers)
- Media query variables no longer resolved → hardcode values
- The `'vars:compiler', 'css'` event is removed

```css
/* Before (CSS Crush): */
.my-element {
    color: $(text-color);
    @media $(mobile) {
        font-size: 14px;
    }
}

/* After (Native CSS): */
.my-element {
    color: var(--elgg-text-color);
    @media (max-width: 820px) {
        font-size: 14px;
    }
}
```

Search for CSS Crush syntax:
```bash
grep -rn '\$(' views/ --include='*.css'
grep -rn 'vars:compiler.*css\|css_compiler' classes/ elgg-plugin.php --include='*.php'
```

Group route definitions dropped the `subpage` variable for these routes:
- `collection:object:blog:group`
- `collection:object:bookmarks:group`
- `collection:object:page:group`

If your plugin generates URLs for these routes with a `subpage` parameter:
```php
// Before:
elgg_generate_url('collection:object:blog:group', [
    'guid' => $group->guid,
    'subpage' => 'all',
]);

// After:
elgg_generate_url('collection:object:blog:group', [
    'guid' => $group->guid,
]);
```

Search:
```bash
grep -rn 'subpage' classes/ views/ --include='*.php' | grep -i 'group\|collection'
```
